 "gender": {
  "rules": [
   "Every noun is masculine, feminine or neuter; grammatical gender only partly follows sex (άνθρωπος is always masc., παιδί, κορίτσι, αγόρι are neuter).",
   "Learn gender with the noun. Nominative singular usually tells it: all masculines end in -ς; almost all feminines in -α or -η; most neuters in -ο, -ι or -μα.",
   "Modifiers agree with the noun's grammatical gender, not the referent's sex: Η Μαρία είναι καλός άνθρωπος.",
   "When sex is unknown or the group is mixed, pronouns and determiners are masculine: Ποιος είναι; Όλοι σας τον ξέρετε.",
   "Numerals used for counting/labels are neuter (η σελίδα τρία) but agree when modifying a noun (τρεις σελίδες).",
   "Common-gender nouns (ο/η πρόεδρος) decline like masculines but take masc. or fem. articles and adjectives by the referent's sex (§3.20)."
  ],
  "examples": [
   {
    "m": "σκύλος",
    "f": "γάτα",
    "n": null,
    "note": "also σκύλα (bitch), γάτος (tomcat)"
   },
