  "final_n_rule": "Feminine accusative τη(ν): the -ν is obligatory before a vowel or κ, π, τ, γκ, μπ, ντ, ξ, ψ (την άνοιξη, την κυρία Αλεξίου) and usually dropped before other consonants (τη Δευτέρα). Indefinite μια(ν): the -ν is optional, used before a vowel or κ, π, τ, ξ, ψ (για μιαν άλλη γυναίκα).",
  "se_contraction": {
   "rule": "σε + definite article fuse into one word",
   "forms": [
    "στον",
    "στη(ν)",
    "στο",
    "στους",
    "στις",
    "στα"
   ],
   "example": {
    "el": "στις όχθες",
    "en": "on the banks"
   }
  },
  "indefinite": {
   "m": {
    "nom": "ένας",
    "acc": "έναν",
    "gen": "ενός"
   },
   "f": {
    "nom": "μια",
    "acc": "μια(ν)",
    "gen": "μιας"
   },
   "n": {
    "nom": "ένα",
    "acc": "ένα",
    "gen": "ενός"
   },
   "notes": [
    "Singular only.",
    "Same as numeral 'one', but the article μια is one syllable; the numeral may be stressed μία (μόνο μία εβδομάδα).",
    "Repeat the article before each noun in a list: ένα μαχαίρι, ένα πιρούνι και μια χαρτοπετσέτα."
   ]
  }
 },
 "declension_rules": [
  "Masculine: vowel + -ς in nom. sg.; acc. sg. drops -ς; gen. sg. = acc. sg., except -ος nouns (gen. -ου).",
  "Feminine (except -ος): nom. = acc. sg., ending in a vowel; gen. sg. adds -ς; nom. = acc. pl., ending in -ς. Feminines in -ος decline like masculine -ος.",
  "Common gender: masculine patterns in -ας, -ης, -ος, -έας.",
  "Neuter: nom. = acc. (= voc.) in each number; plural usually -α (except -ος nouns: -η).",
  "Genitive plural always ends in -ων.",
  "Vocative of feminines and neuters = nominative (feminine -ος nouns normally lack a vocative).",
  "Parisyllabic = same syllable count in sg. and pl. (πατέρας/πατέρες); imparisyllabic = extra syllable in pl. (παπάς/παπάδες)."
 ],
